what would you want to see in a hogwarts  legacy collector's edition  for a franchise as big as harry potter i  feel pretty confident hogwarts legacy  will see at least some form of a  collector's or  special edition all of this of course  when the game launches in  2022 in today's video i'll give you 10  of my favorite ideas for items that  could be included in a hogwarts legacy  collector's edition  also i'll explain why i don't want to  see a wand as part of the package  people love the internet retro racking  tour here and i'm just a dad who loves  games and the stories they tell  we post videos every week here on  youtube and if you want to stay up to  date on all the latest news theories and  discussion regarding hogwarts legacy  then consider subscribing to the channel  and ringing the bell so you don't miss  any of our new videos  video game collector's editions have  grown in popularity over the years and  now it seems  few major games release without one i  know everyone has their own ideas about  what makes a good collector's edition  but for me there are a few things i like  to see now i certainly don't expect a  hogwarts legacy edition to include all  10 items on this list  we'd probably only see a handful of  these items in a package that includes  the game as well of course  for starters though i want to see at  least one item that i can actually  use collectibles figurines they're all  well and good but i prefer the package  include at least  one item that i can use in my everyday  life honestly i  really don't purchase collector's  editions too often but two of my  favorites that i  did end up purchasing number one is the  infamous two collectors edition  and number two is the persona 5  collector's edition  one thing these both had in common is  that they included a bag and i still  have both of them and still  use them even today i'm particularly  fond of the infamous backpack which i  take to work every day and on trips to  hold my electronics  it's of a pretty solid build quality and  has actually held up quite well over all  these years so for number one how about  a hogwarts  storage trunk if any of you out there  own the harry potter  cover boxed set then this idea will be  very familiar to you as that box  set came inside a harry potter storage  trunk now for hogwarts legacy i'd like  to see something that's much  better in quality something closer to  this trunk that you can get from the  pottery barn's online  store they actually have a ton of cool  harry potter items not  sponsored at all by the way i've just  admired their stuff over the years and  have a few items from there of part of  my own collection  this specific trunk that you're seeing  right now actually retails for 350  dollars so it's pretty high quality but  it's also quite  large as you can see in this picture  here now hogwarts legacy could do a much  smaller version of this and even then  it's probably unlikely we'd get  something  that fancy i do think this at least  gives you an idea of what i'm talking  about in terms of a  nice little storage trunk though moving  on to number two i'd love to see a map  of the hogwarts grounds at first i  thought maybe it'd be cool if it  included a map of hogwarts itself but  that would probably prove way too  complex  and then you've got the marauders map  which hadn't been created by the late  1800s time frame in which hogwarts  legacy is set to take place  that being said i think a map of the  grounds would be a fun collectible that  could also be useful to help you  navigate in game i remember red dead  redemption actually packaged a map  inside the regular game as part of the  instruction manual and i really loved  having that  i want to say skyrim did something  similar as well maybe i'm thinking about  another game but i know  hogwarts legacy certainly wouldn't be  the first game to do this for number  three it's true you have to have at  least one collectible trinket type item  in the package and for hogwarts legacy i  would expect at least a few of the  collectibles to be focused on  magical creatures the magical creatures  of the wizarding world have been a  consistent presence in  all of the official material released  about the game from the trailer to the  concept art to the faq  it's clear magical creatures are going  to play a prominent role  with all the magical creatures in the  wizarding world there are numerous  ways they could go with this but i'm  going to go with one of my favorite  creatures in  all of fantasy really and that is a  dragon  i think a dragon statue would be really  fun here maybe they could even  incorporate hogwarts somehow and have  the dragon  flying above like we see in the initial  reveal trailer now almost  any collector's edition out there will  include a soundtrack so that is my  suggestion for number four  the official hogwarts legacy soundtrack  the harry potter series has been  known to have fantastic music throughout  all of the movies and even in the video  games as well  one of the best things about the  hogwarts legacy trailer was the great  music it was really nice and i fully  expect the game to blow  us away when it comes to the music  department  [Applause]  [Music]  so of course we need a full copy to keep  for ourselves and i think it makes  perfect sense to have it as part of a  collector's edition  all right halfway through here and at  number five i'm gonna throw out another  useful item for my suggestion and that  is a hogwarts  satchel or kind of like a tote bag i  talked in the beginning about how i  still use that persona 5 bag and my  infamous backpack so it only makes sense  that i'd like to see  one in hogwarts legacy as well at first  i thought about including house themed  items on the list but with four  different houses i just can't see them  making  four different collectors editions with  a focus on each house  don't get me wrong it'd absolutely be  amazing if they did that but i just  can't see it happening  instead i think it would be smart of  them to focus on items that feature kind  of hogwarts overall  as a school and maybe even the crest  showcasing all four of the houses  at number six no enrollment at hogwarts  is complete without an official  acceptance letter  this would certainly be a smaller item  that could even fit inside the standard  game box but i think it would be a  really nice touch if they included a  little acceptance letter to welcome us  to hogwarts for an  added twist maybe the acceptance letter  could even explain part of the game's  storyline and why we are receiving a  late acceptance letter if you didn't  already know about this it's actually  been confirmed by avalanche that we'll  be starting the game in year five  after receiving a late letter and  personally i really  really want to know why moving on to  number seven one of the items on every  student's supply list is a quill  and parchment i've always wanted to  write with an actual quill and i'm not  talking about a quill that's actually  just a pin  i mean a actual ink bottle and quill  talk about an authentic collector's  edition i'd be blown away if they  managed to include a real quill with a  tiny little bottle of ink  that being said i realized that setting  the bar may be a little bit too high  and truthfully i'd still be happy with  the package that included a quill that's  really just a pin  for number eight i'm gonna suggest  another standard one but one that i  think would be really awesome for  hogwarts legacy and that is an  art book i know i know we see these in  all the collector's editions but just  imagine  how excited we got over four pieces of  concept art that were just released  and in fact really only three one of  them was just kind of the hogwarts house  crests  those three pieces alone have me super  excited for a potential art book i i  really want to see the thought process  and what all of the avalanche artists  have been working on  all this time in preparing for this game  the ones we've seen so far have all been  so incredibly well done and i just know  avalanche has to be sitting on a trove  of pieces  from magical creatures to wands to the  school itself  number nine on our list and once we have  our hogwarts acceptance letter we'll  also need our ticket to platform nine  and three quarters look i know this is a  smaller item but the truth is you're  gonna need some smaller items to kind of  balance out the overall collector's  edition package  anyway you can't have super extravagant  items be the whole thing i mean again  i'd love it but that's just not how  these collector's editions work  a hogwarts acceptance letter paired with  a platform ticket could be the extra  icing on the cake  avalanche could even take this a step  further by having both documents and  maybe a little small  collectible frame or a really nice  sleeve so you can display them together  at number 10 here on our list i'm going  with another big idea  how about a super useful item that would  also fit with heading off to hogwarts  for the start of a new term  how about a hogwarts themed suitcase  like number one on our list the pottery  barn has some incredible harry potter  themed items on that front  they have these right here and they  actually have them for each of the four  houses  now i don't own any of these personally  so i can't speak to their quality but  from what i can see in the images and  reading the description  these appear to have plenty of features  and compartments and i  really love that they have the little  spinner wheels at the bottom always love  seeing people going around the airport  with those little spinning wheels  now in the beginning i mentioned that i  don't want to see a wand as part of the  package and i know that's probably going  to be a thing that a lot of you suggest  but here's why i don't really want to  see it here mainly it's because there  are already  so many really good harry potter style  ones out there already i mean just think  about it over the years between the  books and movies we have seen  numerous different styles we've even got  replicas of the movie ones that have  already been released  if you can ever make it down to the  wizarding world in orlando florida then  you can even get a  personalized wand from ollivanders so at  least for me if they were to include a  wand as part of the collector's edition  then it likely wouldn't come anywhere  close to matching the quality of these  other wands that we've been able to  purchase over the years  now if you can't get enough hogwarts  legacy content i have a full playlist  for you here on the right side of the  screen  and if you're in the mood for some old  school harry potter let's plays then you  can check out the link on the left side  of your screen  as always thank you all so much for  watching i'll talk to you again soon

